Explanation of the change:

- We locate the block where external labels (`element.labelTarget`) get their `color` set via the `element.updateModdleProperties` command.
- The original code always took `di['background-color']` (i.e., the fill) for external labels.
- We replace that with `di['border-color']` so that external labels now use the stroke colour, matching the behaviour for embedded labels.
